{"summary":"Fix payload replacement and preservation during copy-on-write cloning.","explanation":"In Status.TestGetSetPayload, the test sets kUrl1 first to kPayload1 ("aaaaa"), then to kPayload3 ("ccccc"); GetPayload(kUrl1) is expected to return "ccccc" but returns "aaaaa" because SetPayload exits when the URL already exists. In Status.CopyOnWriteForErasePayload, the test copies a status containing the sole kUrl1 payload and expects copy.ErasePayload(kUrl1), then base.ErasePayload(kUrl1), to return true. CloneAndUnref clones payloads only when there are more than one, so both copy-on-write paths discard the sole payload and erase returns false. Updating existing entries and cloning any nonempty payload collection restores both contracts while leaving the empty-payload case unchanged.","edits":[{"path":"absl/status/internal/status_internal.cc","old":"  if (index.has_value()) {
    return;
  }

  payloads_->push_back({std::string(type_url), std::move(payload)});","new":"  if (index.has_value()) {
    (*payloads_)[index.value()].payload = std::move(payload);
    return;
  }

  payloads_->push_back({std::string(type_url), std::move(payload)});"},{"path":"absl/status/internal/status_internal.cc","old":"  if (payloads_ && payloads_->size() > 1) {
    payloads = absl::make_unique<status_internal::Payloads>(*payloads_);
  }","new":"  if (payloads_ && !payloads_->empty()) {
    payloads = absl::make_unique<status_internal::Payloads>(*payloads_);
  }"}]}
